    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "9L81\n1816\nSC\nAAACENTENNIAL*\nE*GKNAPPENBERGERY+·",
      "Welcome Aboard AmericanAirlines\nBeverages\nA choice of spirits and cocktails is available at $1.50\nAmerican beer is available at $1.00\nSpecially selected wines are available at $1.00\nAmerican champagne is available at $1.00\nA selection of cordials is available at $1.50\nTomato Juice, Orange Juice, Coca'Cola and other soft drinks\nFreshly Brewed Coffee, Tea, Milk and Sanka\nWith its origins stretching back as far as those of our nation,\nthe American folk tradition is one that is still a living part of our\nheritage today. The signing of the Declaration of Independence\nin 1776 created a new spirit of unity across the country. As this spirit\nflourished, our own ethnic art grew and became a greater part of\nthe lives of working Americans. Farmers, teachers and tradesmen\nbecame artists in addition to their daily occupations.\nThis patchwork and applique quilt was made in Pennsylvania in\n1876 to celebrate the Centennial of the United States. Courtesy of\nRhea Goodman, Quilt, Inc., New York, New York.\nMenu\nAppetizer\nSpecially chosen to tempt your palate\nand complement your entree selection.\nEntree Selections\nFilet Mignon\nChoice filet mignon,\ncarefully broiled\nserved with fluffy scrambled eggs and\na fresh tomato half.\nEggs Goldenrod\nA lightly grilled corn muffin, topped\nwith egg slices and a creamy\ncheese sauce. Lean\nsmoked\nCanadian bacon.\nManicotti\nTender crepes filled with creamy\nRicotta cheese and baked to\nperfection in a zesty tomato sauce.\nSweet Cake and Butter\nPlease accept our apology if occasionally your selection is not available.\n2006.034.024"
    ],
